{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Lady Hakimah (s.a.), Daughter of Imam al-Jawad (a.s.) — Samarra",
  "data": "At the tomb of Lady Hakimah (s.a.), face the qiblah and recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اٰدَمَ صَفْوَةِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA AADAMA SAFWATILLAAH\nPeace be upon Adam the choice of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى نُوْحٍ نَبِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA NOOHIN NABIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon Noah the prophet of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰىۤ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ خَلِيْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELILLAAH\nPeace be upon Abraham the friend of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُوْسٰى كَلِيْمِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA MOOSAA KALEEMILLAAH\nPeace be upon Moses the spoken by Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عِيْسٰى رُوْحِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA I'EESAA ROOHILLAAH\nPeace be upon Jesus the spirit of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA RASOOLALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَيْرَ خَلْقِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHAYRA KHALQILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s best creature.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَفِيَّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAFIYYALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O elite of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُحَمَّدَ بْنَ عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ خَاتَمَ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUHAMMADABNA A'BDILLAAHI KHAATAMAN NABIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O Muhammad the son of 'Abdullah and the seal of the Prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ عَلِيَّ بْنَ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ وَصِيَّ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA AMEERAL MU'MINEENA A'LIYYABNA ABEE TAALIBIN WASIYYA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O Commander of the Faithful ‘Ali the son of Abu-Talib and the successor of Allah’s Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا فَاطِمَةُ سَيِّدَةَ نِسَاۤءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA FAATIMATU SAYYIDATA NISAA'IL A'ALAMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O Fatimah the doyenne of the women of the worlds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمَا يَا سِبْطَيِ الرَّحْمَةِ وَسَيِّدَيْ شَبَابِ اَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUMAA YAA SIBTAYIR RAHMATI WA SAYYIDAY SHABAABI AHLIL JANNAH\nPeace be upon both of you, O grandsons of the Mercy and two chiefs of the youth of Paradise.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَلِيَّ بْنَ الْحُسَيْنِ سَيِّدَ الْعَابِدِيْنَ وَقُرَّةَ عَيْنِ النَّاظِرِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'LIYYABNAL HUSAYNI SAYYIDAL A'ABIDEENA WA QURRATA A'YNIN NAAZIREEN\nPeace be upon you, O ‘Ali the son of al-Husayn, the chief of the worshippers and the delight of the eye of all seers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُحَمَّدَ بْنَ عَلِيٍّ بَاقِرَ الْعِلْمِ بَعْدَ النَّبِيِّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUHAMMADABNA A'LIYYIN BAAQIRAL I'LMI BA'DAN NABIYY\nPeace be upon you, O Muhammad the son of ‘Ali, the splitter of knowledge after the Prophet.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا جَعْفَرَ بْنَ مُحَمَّدٍ الصَّادِقَ الْبَآرَّ الْاَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA JA'FARABNA MUHAMMADINIS SAADIQAL BAARRAL AMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O Ja'far the son of Muhammad, the veracious, dutiful, and honest.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُوْسَى بْنَ جَعْفَرٍ الطَّاهِرَ الطُّهْرَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MOOSABNA JA'FARINIT TAAHIRAT TUHR\nPeace be upon you, O Musa the son of Ja'far, the immaculate and ever-pure.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَلِيَّ بْنَ مُوْسَى الرِّضَا الْمُرْتَضٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'LIYYABNA MOOSAR RIDAL MURTADAA\nPeace be upon you, O ‘Ali the son of Musa, the well-pleased and well-contented.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُحَمَّدَ بْنَ عَلِيٍّ التَّقِيَّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUHAMMADABNA A'LIYYINIT TAQIYY\nPeace be upon you, O Muhammad the son of ‘Ali, the pious.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَلِيَّ بْنَ مُحَمَّدٍ النَّقِيَّ النَّاصِحَ الْاَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'LIYYABNA MUHAMMADININ NAQIYYAN NAASIHAL AMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O ‘Ali the son of Muhammad, the immaculate, sincere, and honest.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حَسَنَ بْنَ عَلِيٍّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HASANABNA A'LIYY\nPeace be upon you, O Hasan the son of ‘Ali.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْوَصِيِّ مِنْ بَعْدِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL WASIYYI MIN BA'DIH\nPeace be upon the next successor.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى نُوْرِكَ وَسِرَاجِكَ وَوَلِيِّ وَلِيِّكَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA NOORIKA WA SIRAAJIKA WA WALIYYI WALIYYIK\nO Allah, send blessings upon Your light, Your lantern, the representative of Your representative,\nوَوَصِيِّ وَصِيِّكَ وَحُجَّتِكَ عَلٰى خَلْقِكَ\nWA WASIYYI WASIYYIKA WA HUJJATIKA A'LAA KHALQIK\nthe successor of Your successor, and the argument of You against Your creatures.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا بِنْتَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA BINTA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O daughter of Allah’s Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا بِنْتَ فَاطِمَةَ وَخَدِيْجَةَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA BINTA FAATIMATA WA KHADEEJAH\nPeace be upon you, O daughter of Fatimah and Khadijah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا بِنْتَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA BINTA AMEERIL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon you, O daughter of the Commander of the Faithful.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا بِنْتَ الْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA BINTAL HASANI WAL HUSAYN\nPeace be upon you, O daughter of al-Hasan and al-Husayn.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا بِنْتَ وَلِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA BINTA WALIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O daughter of Allah’s representative.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا اُخْتَ وَلِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA UKHTA WALIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O sister of Allah’s representative.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا عَمَّةَ وَلِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA A'MMATA WALIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O paternal aunt of Allah’s representative.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا بِنْتَ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ التَّقِيِّ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA BINTA MUHAMMADIBNI A'LIYYINIT TAQIYYI WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you, O daughter of Muhammad the son of ‘Ali, the pious. Allah’s mercy and blessings, too, be upon you.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ عَرَّفَ اللّٰهُ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ فِي الْجَنَّةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI A'RRAFALLAAHU BAYNANAA WA BAYNAKUM FIL JANNAH\nPeace be upon you. May Allah introduce us to you all in Paradise,\nوَحَشَرَنَا فِيْ زُمْرَتِكُمْ وَاَوْرَدَنَا حَوْضَ نَبِيِّكُمْ\nWA HASHARANAA FEE ZUMRATIKUM WA AWRADANAA HAWDA NABIYYIKUM\ninclude us with your group, allow us to approach the pond of your Prophet,\nوَسَقَانَا بِكَاْسِ جَدِّكُمْ مِنْ يَدِ عَلِيِّ بْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ\nWA SAQAANAA BIKA'SI JADDIKUM MIN YADI A'LIYYIBNI ABEE TAALIB\nand serve us with water from the cup of your grandfather and from the hand of ‘Ali the son of Abu-Talib.\nصَلَوَاتُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ\nSALAWAATULLAAHI A'LAYKUM\nAllah’s blessings be upon you all.\nاَسْاَلُ اللّٰهَ اَنْ يُرِيَنَا فِيْكُمُ السُّرُوْرَ وَالْفَرَجَ\nAS'ALULLAAHA AN YURIYANAA FEEKUMUS SUROORA WAL FARAJ\nI beseech Allah to show us delight and relief through you,\nوَاَنْ يَجْمَعَنَا وَاِيَّاكُمْ فِيْ زُمْرَةِ جَدِّكُمْ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nWA AN YAJMA'ANAA WA IYYAAKUM FEE ZUMRATI JADDIKUM MUHAMMADIN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nto join us with you in the group of your grandfather Muhammad, Allah’s blessings be upon him and his Household,\nوَاَنْ لَا يَسْلُبَنَا مَعْرِفَتَكُمْ اِنَّهٗ وَلِيٌّ قَدِيْرٌ\nWA AN LAA YASLUBANAA MA'RIFATAKUM INNAHOO WALIYYUN QADEER\nand never to deprive us of our recognition of you. Verily, He is Guardian and All-powerful.\nاَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ بِحُبِّكُمْ وَالْبَرَاۤءَةِ مِنْ اَعْدَاۤئِكُمْ\nATAQARRABU ILALLAAHI BIHUBBIKUM WAL BARAA'ATI MIN A'DAA'IKUM\nI seek nearness to Allah through my love for you, repudiation of your enemies,\nوَالتَّسْلِيْمِ اِلَى اللّٰهِ رَاضِيًا بِهٖ غَيْرَ مُنْكِرٍ وَلَا مُسْتَكْبِرٍ\nWAT TASLEEMI ILALLAAHI RAADIYAN BIHEE GHAYRA MUNKIRIN WA LAA MUSTAKBIR\nand submission to Allah, accepting Him without denial or arrogance,\nوَعَلٰى يَقِيْنِ مَاۤ اَتٰى بِهٖ مُحَمَّدٌ وَبِهٖ رَاضٍ\nWA A'LAA YAQEENI MAA ATAA BIHEE MUHAMMADUN WA BIHEE RAAD\nbeing fully certain of what Muhammad has brought and showing full satisfaction with it.\nنَطْلُبُ بِذٰلِكَ وَجْهَكَ يَا سَيِّدِيْ اَللّٰهُمَّ وَرِضَاكَ وَالدَّارَ الْاٰخِرَةَ\nNATLUBU BIDHAALIKA WAJHAKA YAA SAYYIDEE ALLAAHUMMA WA RIDAAKA WAD DAARAL AAKHIRAH\nWe, through this, only seek Your Face, O my Master Allah, and Your satisfaction as well as the Next Abode.\nيَا حَكِيْمَةُ اشْفَعِيْ لِيْ فِي الْجَنَّةِ\nYAA HAKEEMATUSH FA'EE LEE FIL JANNAH\nO Hakimah, (please) intercede for me to win Paradise,\nفَاِنَّ لَكِ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ شَاْنًا مِنَ الشَّاْنِ\nFA-INNA LAKI I'NDALLAAHI SHA'NAN MINASH SHA'N\nfor you enjoy an outstanding status with Allah.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيۤ اَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تَخْتِمَ لِيْ بِالسَّعَادَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA AN TAKHTIMA LEE BIS SA'AADAH\nO Allah, I do beseech You to seal my life with happiness;\nفَلَا تَسْلُبْ مِنِّيْ مَا اَنَا فِيْهِ\nFALAA TASLUB MINNEE MAA ANAA FEEH\nso, (please) do not deprive me of that which I enjoy.\nوَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEM\nThere is neither might nor power except with Allah the All-high and All-great.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اسْتَجِبْ لَنَا وَتَقَبَّلْهُ بِكَرَمِكَ وَعِزَّتِكَ وَبِرَحْمَتِكَ وَعَافِيَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMAS TAJIB LANAA WA TAQABBALHU BIKARAMIKA WA I'ZZATIKA WA BIRAHMATIKA WA A'AFIYATIK\nO Allah, (please) respond to us and accept this from us in the name of Your generosity, almightiness, mercy, and bestowal of wellbeing.\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهٖ اَجْمَعِيْنَ وَسَلَّمَ تَسْلِيْمًا\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE AJMA'EENA WA SALLAMA TASLEEMAA\nMay Allah bless Muhammad and his entire Household and pour down peace on them,\nيَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most merciful of all those who show mercy.",
  "merits": "Zayd al-Shahham asked Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.), \"What is the reward of one who visits one of you (the Ahl al-Bayt)?\" The Imam (a.s.) answered, \"It is like visiting the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w.a.).\" Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is also reported to have said that whoever offers a four-unit prayer at the tomb of an Imam whose obedience is obligatory shall have the reward of a hajj and an 'umrah.\n\nLady Hakimah (s.a.), the daughter of Imam Muhammad al-Taqi al-Jawad (a.s.), is buried in the shrine of the two Imams (a.s.) at Samarra: her tomb lies behind their feet and is joined to their tombs. Shaykh Abbas Qummi, who gives her merits in his Hadiyyat al-Za'irin, writes that the books of ziyarat record no ziyarat for her in particular, high as her standing is. So she is visited with the general ziyarat of the Imams' descendants, or with the ziyarat of her paternal aunt Lady Fatimah al-Masumah, the daughter of Imam Musa al-Kazim (a.s.), the [Ziyarat of Lady Masuma (s.a.)](G78), with Lady Hakimah's own names in it. That is the ziyarat given here."
}
